11.
Power and duties of Secretary.
- The Secretary of the committee shall-
(a)
be the Chief Executive authority of the committee and responsible for carrying out its decisions;
(b)
represent the committee in all suits and proceedings for and against the committee;
(c)
authenticate by his signature all decisions and instructions of the committee;
(d)
operate the bank accounts of the committee jointly with the Treasurer;
(e)
convene meetings of the committee and prepare its minutes;
(f)
attend the meetings of the committee with all the necessary records and information;
(g)
maintain such forms, registers and other records as may be prescribed, from time to time, and do all correspondence
relating to the committee;
(h)
prepare an annual statement of business transacted by the committee during each financial year; and
(i)
do such other acts as may be directed by the committee and the Bar Council.
